      "title": "Case-delete client mutation",
      "summary": "A useMutation hook that DELETEs /v1/cases/:slug and invalidates the cases-listing query once the delete is accepted.",
      "task": "task/case-deletion-surface/delete-case-mutation"
    },
    {
      "id": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-delete-refusal-presentation",
      "kind": "proof",
      "file": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-delete-refusal-presentation.md",
      "title": "Refusal presentation for a case delete on the case detail surface",
      "summary": "Tests over CaseDetailScreen's rendered delete dialog proving each of the three distinguishable, disclosure-appropriate refusal statements this task wires (CaseHoldsVersionsError, CaseNotFoundError, any other code), their mutual distinctness, and that the cases listing still carries the refused case's own slug.",
      "task": "task/case-deletion-surface/case-delete-refusal-presentation"
    },
    {
      "id": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-detail-delete-control",
      "kind": "proof",
      "file": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-detail-delete-control.md",
      "title": "Delete control on the case detail surface for a case holding no version",
      "summary": "Frontend tests for the slug-confirmed delete dialog on CaseDetailScreen -- its conditional visibility, the further explicit act it requires before issuing a DELETE, exactly one DELETE under a double click, the post-accept navigation to the cases listing, and the listing's own state once the delete is accepted -- with the accepted-delete statement question left untested rather than pinned either way.",
      "task": "task/case-deletion-surface/case-detail-delete-control"
    },
    {
      "id": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-holds-versions-error-state",
      "kind": "proof",
      "file": "proof/case-deletion-surface/case-holds-versions-error-state.md",
      "title": "CaseHoldsVersionsError gets a distinct, non-generic UI error-state kind",
      "summary": "Proves that uiStateForApiError now answers CaseHoldsVersionsError with a kind of its own, distinct from every other code the map names (including case-not-found) and from the generic fallback, while the case-not-found and unnamed-code paths remain exactly as they answered before.",
      "task": "task/case-deletion-surface/case-holds-versions-error-state"
    },
    {
      "id": "proof/case-deletion-surface/delete-case-mutation",
      "kind": "proof",
      "file": "proof/case-deletion-surface/delete-case-mutation.md",
      "title": "Case-delete client mutation proof",
      "summary": "Six tests over useDeleteCase pin the wire request it issues, its 204-success settlement and cache invalidation, its 409/404 error-code pass-through, and the underdetermined boundary that keeps an unnamed refusal's own wire code rather than folding it into CaseNotFoundError.",
      "task": "task/case-deletion-surface/delete-case-mutation"
    },
    {
      "id": "review/case-deletion-frontend",
      "kind": "review",
      "file": "review/case-deletion-frontend.md",
      "title": "Review of case-deletion-frontend",
      "summary": "Coverage, conformance, standard and failures passes over the case-deletion-frontend delivery: a slug-confirmed delete control on the case detail surface for a case holding no version, landing on the cases listing once accepted, and presenting the CaseHoldsVersionsError, CaseNotFoundError and unrecognised refusals distinctly.",
      "ran": [
        "coverage",
        "conformance",
        "standard"
      ],
      "unproven": [
        "A delete answered with HTTP 409 CaseHoldsVersionsError is presented to the curator as the case holding a version and not having been deleted.",
        "A delete refused with any error code other than CaseHoldsVersionsError or CaseNotFoundError is presented as a failure distinct from both of those refusals.",
        "A succeeded mutation invalidates the query backing the cases listing.",
        "After a delete answered with HTTP 409 CaseHoldsVersionsError, the cases listing still carries an entry for that slug.",
        "After the delete is answered with HTTP 204, the cases listing carries no entry for the deleted slug.",
        "After the delete is answered with HTTP 204, the cases listing still carries an entry for every other case it carried before the delete."
      ],
      "findings": 3
    }
  ],
